#[[

When `MainModel` declares `InnerComponent<ContentModel>`, the framework resolves the implementation with the **highest** priority — `TableContentModel` in this case.
To switch to the list view, simply change the priority levels.
This mechanism allows you to swap UI implementations without modifying any consumer code.

Both implementations share the same pattern:

1. `@Link` the `TodoService` to access data
2. In `bind()`, create a `FilteredList` wrapping the service's observable list and set it on the view's table/list
3. Listen for `UPDATE_STATUS` waves to refresh the filter predicate


## Service Layer — TodoService

The service layer follows the JRebirth interface/implementation split.
The interface declares wave contracts; the implementation does the work.

### The interface

]]#


```java
package org.jrebirth.af.showcase.todos.service;

import static org.jrebirth.af.core.wave.WBuilder.waveType;

import org.jrebirth.af.api.module.RegistrationPoint;
import org.jrebirth.af.api.service.Service;
import org.jrebirth.af.api.wave.Wave;
import org.jrebirth.af.api.wave.contract.WaveItem;
import org.jrebirth.af.api.wave.contract.WaveType;
import org.jrebirth.af.core.wave.JRebirthItems;
import org.jrebirth.af.core.wave.WaveItemBase;
import org.jrebirth.af.showcase.todos.bean.Todo;
import org.jrebirth.af.showcase.todos.bean.TodoList;

import javafx.beans.property.StringProperty;

/**
 * The interface <strong>TodoService</strong>.
 *
 * @author Sébastien Bordes
 */
@RegistrationPoint
public interface TodoService extends Service {

    String ADDED = "ADDED";

    String REMOVED = "REMOVED";

    WaveItem<StringProperty> TODO_STRING = new WaveItemBase<StringProperty>() {
    };

    WaveItem<Todo> TODO = new WaveItemBase<Todo>() {
    };

    // WaveItem<List<TodoList>> RESULT = new WaveItemBase<List<TodoList>>() {
    // };

    WaveType DO_ADD = waveType("ADD")
                                     .items(TODO_STRING)
                                     .returnItem(JRebirthItems.booleanItem)
                                     .returnAction(ADDED);

    WaveType DO_REMOVE = waveType("REMOVE")
                                           .items(TODO)
                                           .returnItem(JRebirthItems.booleanItem)
                                           .returnAction(REMOVED);

    boolean doAdd(final StringProperty text, final Wave wave);

    boolean doRemove(final Todo todo, final Wave wave);

    TodoList getTodoList();
}
```

#[[

Key elements:

- **`@RegistrationPoint`** marks this as the injection target — consumers `@Link` the interface, not the implementation.
- **`WaveItem`** declarations (`TODO_STRING`, `TODO`) define the typed payload slots carried by waves.
- **`WaveType`** declarations (`DO_ADD`, `DO_REMOVE`) define the wave contracts, including which items they carry and what they return.
- The `returnAction(ADDED)` clause means that after `doAdd` completes, JRebirth automatically fires a return wave with action name `"ADDED"`, carrying the boolean result.

### The implementation

]]#


```java
package org.jrebirth.af.showcase.todos.service;

import org.jrebirth.af.api.module.Register;
import org.jrebirth.af.api.wave.Wave;
import org.jrebirth.af.core.service.DefaultService;
import org.jrebirth.af.showcase.todos.bean.Todo;
import org.jrebirth.af.showcase.todos.bean.TodoList;

import javafx.beans.property.StringProperty;

@Register(value = TodoService.class)
public class TodoServiceImpl extends DefaultService implements TodoService {

    private final TodoList todoList = new TodoList();

    /**
     * @return Returns the todoList.
     */
    @Override
    public TodoList getTodoList() {
        return this.todoList;
    }

    @Override
    public boolean doAdd(final StringProperty text, final Wave wave) {

        this.todoList.addTodo(Todo.of().text(text.getValue()).done(false));

        return true;
    }

    @Override
    public boolean doRemove(final Todo todo, final Wave wave) {

        this.todoList.removeTodo(todo);

        return true;
    }

}
```

#[[

`@Register(value = TodoService.class)` tells the framework to register this class under the `TodoService` interface.
Any component that does `@Link private TodoService todoService;` will receive this implementation.

The `doAdd` and `doRemove` methods follow the JRebirth naming convention: a `WaveType` named `DO_ADD` maps to a method `doAdd`.
The framework dispatches incoming waves to the matching method automatically.


## Wave Communication — WWaves

Application-level wave types are gathered in a `WWaves` interface.

]]#


```java
package org.jrebirth.af.showcase.todos.ui;

import org.jrebirth.af.api.annotation.Preload;
import org.jrebirth.af.api.wave.contract.WaveType;
import org.jrebirth.af.core.wave.WBuilder;

@Preload
public interface WWaves {

    String UPDATE_STATUS = "UPDATE_STATUS";
    WaveType UPDATE_STATUS_WT = WBuilder.waveType(UPDATE_STATUS);
}
```

#[[

The `@Preload` annotation tells JRebirth to initialize this interface's static fields at startup, before any model is created.
This avoids class-loading race conditions.

`UPDATE_STATUS_WT` is a simple notification wave with no payload.
When the status bar filter changes, it sends this wave; both `TableContentModel` and `ListContentModel` listen for it via `@OnWave(WWaves.UPDATE_STATUS)` and refresh their filtered views.

### Wave flow in action

Here is the typical lifecycle of an "add todo" operation:

1. User types text in the header and presses Enter.
2. `HeaderController` captures the key event and delegates to `HeaderModel`.
3. `HeaderModel` calls `todoService.doAdd(text, wave)` — but since `doAdd` is a wave-type method, it actually sends a `DO_ADD` wave.
4. `TodoServiceImpl.doAdd()` executes on the JRebirth Thread Pool, adds the `Todo` to the `TodoList`.
5. The `TodoList` (generated from Ecore) is an observable list — the `TableView` / list view updates automatically.
6. The return wave `ADDED` fires, and any listener can react.


## Resource Declarations

JRebirth provides enum-based resource management for fonts, images, and stylesheets.
Resources are resolved from the classpath using a convention-over-configuration approach.

### Fonts

]]#


```java
package org.jrebirth.af.showcase.todos.resource;

import org.jrebirth.af.api.resource.font.FontExtension;
import org.jrebirth.af.core.resource.font.FontEnum;

/**
 * The TodosFonts enumeration providing all fonts.
 */
public enum TodosFonts implements FontEnum {

    // @formatter:off

    /** The font used to display delete icon. */
    DELETE {{ real(TodosFontNames.fontello, 16.0, FontExtension.TTF); }};

}
```

