```

#[[

Each resource type follows the same pattern:

- Declare an `enum` (or `interface` for stylesheets) that implements the corresponding JRebirth resource type (`FontEnum`, `ImageEnum`, `StyleSheetItem`).
- Use the initializer block to specify the resource name, extension, and any parameters (font size, image path, etc.).
- Reference the resource in code via the enum constant — e.g., `TodosImages.HEADER_LOGO.get()` returns a JavaFX `Image`.

JRebirth handles classpath resolution, caching, and JPMS module boundaries transparently.


## Ecore Code Generation

The `Todo` and `TodoList` beans are not written by hand — they are generated from an Ecore model.

The `Todos.ecore` file defines two classes:

- **`Todo`** with `text` (String) and `done` (boolean) attributes
- **`TodoList`** with a multi-valued `todo` reference to `Todo`

The `jrebirth-maven-plugin` transforms this Ecore model into JavaFX beans with full property support:
each attribute becomes a JavaFX `Property` (e.g., `textProperty()`, `doneProperty()`),
and list references become `ObservableList` fields (e.g., `pTodo()` returns an `ObservableList<Todo>`).

This is why the `FilteredList` in the content models can wrap `todoService.getTodoList().pTodo()` directly — it's a live observable list.


## Key Patterns Summary

| Pattern | Where | Why |
|---------|-------|-----|
| Inner components (`@Link InnerComponent<T>`) | `MainModel` | Compose UI from independent, lifecycle-managed sub-models |
| Interface + `@Register` | `TodoService` / `TodoServiceImpl` | Decouple contract from implementation; enable DI |
| Multiple implementations via priority | `TableContentModel` / `ListContentModel` | Swap UI implementations without changing consumers |
| Wave contracts (`WaveType`, `WaveItem`) | `TodoService`, `WWaves` | Type-safe, decoupled asynchronous messaging |
| `@OnWave` annotation | `ListContentModel.updateStatus()` | Declarative wave listening on model methods |
| Resource enums | `TodosFonts`, `TodosImages`, `TodosStyles` | Classpath-resolved, cached, JPMS-aware resources |
| Ecore → JavaFX beans | `Todos.ecore` → `Todo`, `TodoList` | Generated observable beans with property support |

